-- title:
--   Theorem 3.1(a) — one-step inequality (10) for DCAe
-- statement:
--   Let $f,g,h,\varphi,L,l$ satisfy Assumption 1, let $\delta\in(0,1)$, and let $(x^k)$ be generated by DCAe (with extrapolation parameters $\beta_k$ satisfying (8) and $\xi^k\in\partial h(x^k)$). Then for $k=0,1,\dots$
--
--   $$
--   F(x^{k+1}) \le F(x^k) + \delta L\,D_\varphi(x^{k-1},x^k) - L\,D_\varphi(x^k,x^{k+1}),
--   $$
--
--   with $x^{-1}=x^0$. This is the basic descent estimate behind the subsequential and global convergence analysis.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Stated as $F(x^{k+1})+L\,D_\varphi(x^k,x^{k+1})\le F(x^k)+\delta L\,D_\varphi(x^{k-1},x^k)$ in `EReal`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: E a finite dimensional real linear space with inner product ⟨·,·⟩ and norm ‖·‖ → any finite-dimensional real inner product space E; reason: the paper uses ⟨·,·⟩ and ‖·‖ on E; same instances
--   - encoding: g : E → (−∞, +∞] and F = f + g − h extended-real → g and F valued in EReal; reason: Lean convention; f and h are real so no ∞ − ∞ occurs; same instances
--   - encoding: x^{−1} := x^0 (initialization of Algorithm 1) → x : ℕ → E and prev x 0 = x 0, prev x (k+1) = x k; reason: the convention is built into prev; same runs
--   - reading: Assumption 1(b) g : E → R ∩ {+∞} → g : E → EReal, proper (never −∞, not identically +∞), lsc, convex; reason: R ∩ {+∞} is empty; the intended codomain is R ∪ {+∞}, as in §2 (p.4)
--   - reading: (9) prints ⟨Lφ(y^k) − ∇f(y^k) + ξ^k, x⟩ → ⟨L∇φ(y^k) − ∇f(y^k) + ξ^k, x⟩; reason: Lφ(y^k) is a number where a vector is needed; the text above Algorithm 1 (∇Lφ(y^k)) and the proof of Theorem 3.1 (L∇φ(y^k)) give the only well-typed reading
--   - reading: β_k is the extrapolation parameter satisfying (8); the proofs on pp.7 and 9 use 0 ≤ β_k < 1 → β_k any real satisfying (8); reason: Algorithm 1 imposes only (8); adding 0 ≤ β_k < 1 would be the weaker reading, and strong convexity of φ with (8) gives the bounds on ‖y^k − x^k‖ the proofs need
--   - encoding: (10) F(x^{k+1}) ≤ F(x^k) + δLD_φ(x^{k−1}, x^k) − LD_φ(x^k, x^{k+1}) → the same inequality in additive form, with both Bregman terms moved to the side where they are added; reason: the left side may be +∞ (x^0 ∉ dom g is allowed); for finite values the forms are equivalent
-- source:
--   Phan, Le Thi, DCA based algorithm with extrapolation for nonconvex nonsmooth optimization, arXiv:2106.04743v1, Theorem 3.1(a), p.6, (10)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DCAExtrap_Assumption1
import Definitions.Def_DCAExtrap_IsDCAeRun

namespace DCAExtrap

/-- **Theorem 3.1(a)** (Phan–Le Thi, arXiv:2106.04743v1, p.6, inequality (10)). Let `{x^k}` be
the sequence generated by DCAe and suppose Assumption 1 holds. Then for `k = 0, 1, …`
`F(x^{k+1}) ≤ F(x^k) + δ L D_φ(x^{k−1}, x^k) − L D_φ(x^k, x^{k+1})`.

**Formalization Note.** `E` is any finite-dimensional real inner product space. `F` is
`EReal`-valued, so (10) is stated in the additive form
`F(x^{k+1}) + L D_φ(x^k, x^{k+1}) ≤ F(x^k) + δ L D_φ(x^{k−1}, x^k)` (both Bregman terms are
real); at `k = 0` with `x^0 ∉ dom g` the right side is `+∞`. `x^{−1} = x^0` through `prev`.
`β_k` is any real satisfying (8) and `ξ^k` any element of `∂h(x^k)`. -/
theorem theorem_3_1_a {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {f : E → ℝ} {g : E → EReal} {h : E → ℝ} {φ : E → ℝ} {L l δ : ℝ}
    {x : ℕ → E} {β : ℕ → ℝ} {ξ : ℕ → E}
    (hA1 : Assumption1 f g h φ L l) (hrun : IsDCAeRun f g h φ L l δ x β ξ) (k : ℕ) :
    objF f g h (x (k + 1)) + ((L * bregman φ (x k) (x (k + 1)) : ℝ) : EReal) ≤
      objF f g h (x k) + ((δ * L * bregman φ (prev x k) (x k) : ℝ) : EReal) := by sorry

end DCAExtrap
